    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d133-a6">

                <pb facs="0282" n="226" xml:id="pg226"/>


                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">In
                                the High Court of Justice</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Queen’s Bench Division</hi></placeName>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">In the matter of Ezra D. Winslow, a prisoner in the house of
                    detentiou under the extradition warrant of commitment.</p>
                <p>We hereby give you notice that we shall to-morrow, at 12 o’clock, apply to a
                    judge at chambers, by counsel, for an order for the discharge of the above-named
                    Ezra Dyer Winslow, or for a writ <hi rendition="#italic">of habeas corpus</hi>
                    directing the governor of the house of detention, Clerkenwell, in the county of
                    Middlesex, to bring up the body of Ezra Dyer Winslow, in order that he may be
                    discharged from custody, he having been in custody under an extradition warrant
                    of committal since 3d March last.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">Dated <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1876-05-02">this 2d day of May, 1876</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/> Yours, &amp;c.,<lb/><signed>WONTNER &amp; SONS</signed>,<lb/>3 <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cloak Lane, Canada Street, Solicitors for the said Ezra
                        Dyer Winslow</hi>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
